// The slots package: SlotTable[T] is now GenPool[T] of the pools package, and
// Slot is its Handle. They stay here as aliases for one release so that the
// users of SlotTable can move to the pools package one at a time; nothing else
// is left in this package. Read pools/src/pools.cone for what a table does.
//
//   SlotTable[T]   GenPool[T]
//   Slot           a Handle: cell index and generation
//
// A GenPool keeps its cells in one growable block, not slabs, so there is no
// per-slab sizing and no slab goes back to the C library while the table lives;
// the block grows (and may move) as cells are added. A cell whose generation
// would wrap is retired for good rather than wrapping.
// New in the table: retire, free, retireAt, freeAt, iter, entries, nextLive.

mod slots;

import pools pub use GenPool as SlotTable, Handle as Slot;

